  "result": "adenosine triphosphate disodium (CHEBI:50732) (https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A50732)\nciteturn77search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; adenosine triphosphate disodium (CHEBI:50732) is a organic sodium salt (CHEBI:38700)\n\n## CHEBI:50732 - adenosine triphosphate disodium\n\nImage: Default Structure\n\nTake structure to advanced search\n\nChEBI ID  | CHEBI:50732\nChEBI Name  | adenosine triphosphate disodium\nStars  | \nLast Modified  | 30 September 2008\nSubmitter  | Inma Spiteri\nDownloads  | Molfile\n\nFormula  | C10H14N5O13P3.2Na\nNet Charge  | 0\nAverage Mass  | 551.146\nMonoisotopic Mass  | 550.95963\nSMILES  | Nc1ncnc2c1ncn2[C@@H]1O[C@H](COP(=O)(O)OP(=O)(O)OP(=O)([O-])[O-])[C@@H](O)[C@H]1O.[Na+].[Na+]\nInChI  | InChI=1S/C10H16N5O13P3.2Na/c11-8-5-9(13-2-12-8)15(3-14-5)10-7(17)6(16)4(26-10)1-25-30(21,22)28-31(23,24)27-29(18,19)20;;/h2-4,6-7,10,16-17H,1H2,(H,21,22)(H,23,24)(H2,11,12,13)(H2,18,19,20);;/q;2*+1/p-2/t4-,6-,7-,10-;;/m1../s1\nInChIKey  | TTWYZDPBDWHJOR-IDIVVRGQSA-L\n\nChEBI Ontology\n---\n\nText\n\nTree View\n\nGraph View\n\nOutgoing Relation(s)\nadenosine triphosphate disodium (CHEBI:50732) has part ({[(2R,3S,4R,5R)-3,4-dihydroxy-5-(9H-purin-9-yl)oxolan-2-yl]methyl phosphonato}oxy)(phosphonatooxy)phosphinate (CHEBI:237958)\nadenosine triphosphate disodium (CHEBI:50732) has part ATP (CHEBI:15422)\nadenosine triphosphate disodium (CHEBI:50732) is a organic sodium salt (CHEBI:38700)\n\nIUPAC Name \n---\ndisodium 5'-O-(hydroxy{[hydroxy(phosphonatooxy)phosphoryl]oxy}phosphoryl)adenosine\n\nSynonym s   | Source\n--- | ---\nAdenosine 5'-triphosphate disodium salt  | ChemIDplus\nDisodium adenosine 5'-triphosphate  | ChemIDplus\n\nBrand Name   | Source\n--- | ---\nStriadyne  | DrugBank\n\nManual Xrefs  | Databases\n--- | ---\nDB00171  | DrugBank\n\nRegistry Numbers  | Sources\n--- | ---\nCAS:987-65-5  | ChemIDplus--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nScreening assessment for EDTA and its salts group - Canada.ca (https://www.canada.ca/en/environment-climate-change/services/evaluating-existing-substances/screening-assessment-edta-salts.html)\nciteturn77search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.5 years ago; Crawled: today; CAS RN 60-00-4 is EDTA and has four acetic acid groups, CAS RN 64-02-8 is a sodium salt of EDTA, CAS RN 15708-41-5 is a ferric salt of EDTA, and CAS RN 21265-50-9 is a ferric ammonium salt of EDTA.\n\n# Final screening assessment for EDTA and its salts group\n\nChemical Abstracts Service Registry Numbers\n60-00-4\n64-02-8\n15708-41-5\n21265-50-9\n\nEnvironment and Climate Change Canada\n\nHealth Canada\n\nMay 2018\n\n## Synopsis\n\nPursuant to sections 68 or 74 of the Canadian Environmental Protection Act, 1999 (CEPA), the Minister of the Environment and the Minister of Health have conducted a screening assessment of four substances referred to collectively as the EDTA and its salts group. Although there are other EDTA salts, substances in this group were identified as priorities for assessment as they met categorization criteria under subsection 73(1) of CEPA or were considered a priority on the basis of other human health concerns. The Chemical Abstracts Service Registry Numbers (CAS RN^{Footnote 1} , their Domestic Substances List (DSL) names and their common names are listed in the table below.\n\nSubstances in the EDTA and its salts group\nChemical Abstracts Service Registry Numbers  | Domestic Substances List name  | Common names\n60-00-4^{ }  | Glycine, N,N′-1,2-ethanediylbis[N-(carboxymethyl)-  | Ethylene diaminetetraacetic acid (EDTA) or edetic acid\n64-02-8  | Glycine, N,N′-1,2-ethanediylbis[N-(carboxymethyl)-, tetrasodium Salt  | Tetrasodium EDTA\n15708-41-5^{a}  | Ferrate(1-), [[N,N′-1,2-ethanediylbis[N- (carboxymethyl)glycinato]](4-)-N,N′,O,O′,ON,ON′]-, sodium, (OC-6-21)-  | Ferric monosodium EDTA\n21265-50-9^{a}  | Ferrate(1-), [[N,N′-1,2-ethanediylbis[N- (carboxymethyl)glycinato]](4-)-N,N′,O,O′,ON,ON′]-, ammonium, (OC-6-21)-  | Ferric ammonium EDTA\n\n^{a }This substance was not identified under subsection 73(1) of CEPA but was included in this assessment as it was considered a priority on the basis of other human health concerns.\n\nThe four substances in this group do not occur naturally in the environment. Some of them are primarily used as chelating agents or preservatives in cleaning products, cosmetics, prescription and non-prescription drugs, natural health products, and products used by consumers. Other uses include manufacture of products for printing inks, paints and coatings, ion exchange agents, automotive care, water treatment, food packaging, and pest control. \nThis screening assessment focuses on information critical to determining whether substances meet the criteria as set out in section 64 of CEPA by examining scientific information and incorporating a weight-of-evidence approach and precaution.^{Footnote 2}  This screening assessment presents the critical information and considerations on which the conclusion is based.\n\n## 2. Identity of substances\n\nThe Chemical Abstracts Service Registry Numbers (CAS RN^{Footnote 3} ), Domestic Substances List (DSL) names and common names and/or acronyms for the individual substances in the EDTA and its salts group are presented in Table 2‑1.\n\nThe four substances within this group all have the same ethylenediamine backbone with carboxylic acid groups on the amine that enable chelation or sequestration of metal ions. CAS RN 60-00-4 is EDTA and has four acetic acid groups, CAS RN 64-02-8 is a sodium salt of EDTA, CAS RN 15708-41-5 is a ferric salt of EDTA, and CAS RN 21265-50-9 is a ferric ammonium salt of EDTA.\n\nSubstance identities\n\nChemical Abstracts Service Registry Numbers (acronym): 60-00-4 (EDTA)\n\nDomestic Substances List (common name):\nGlycine, N,N′-1,2-ethanediylbis[N-(carboxymethyl)-\n(EDTA or Edetic acid)\n\nChemical structure and molecular formula\n\nImage\n\nC_{10}H_{16}N_{2}O_{8}\n\nMolecular weight^{ a  }(g/mol): 292.25\n\nChemical Abstracts Service Registry Numbers (acronym): 64-02-8 (Na_{4}EDTA)\n\nDomestic Substances List (common name):\nGlycine, N,N′-1,2-ethanediylbis[N-(carboxymethyl)-, tetrasodium salt\n(Tetrasodium EDTA)\n\nChemical structure and molecular formula\n\nImage\n\nC_{10}H_{12}N_{2}Na_{4}O_{8}\n\nMolecular weight^{ a  }(g/mol): 380.17\n\nChemical Abstracts Service Registry Numbers (acronym): 15708-41-5 [Fe(III)NaEDTA]\n\nDomestic Substances List (common name):\nFerrate(1-), [[N,N′-1,2-ethanediylbis[N-(carboxymethyl)glycinato]](4-)-N,N′,O,O′,ON,ON′]-,  sodium, (OC-6-21)-\n(Ferric monosodium EDTA)\n\nChemical structure and molecular formula\n\nImage\n\nC_{10}H_{12}FeN_{2}O_{8.}Na\n\nMolecular weight^{ a  }(g/mol): 367.05\n\nChemical Abstracts Service Registry Numbers (acronym): 21265-50-9 [Fe(III)(NH_{4})EDTA]\n\nDomestic Substances List (common name):\nFerrate(1-), [[N,N′-1,2-ethanediylbis[N-(carboxymethyl)glycinato]](4-)-N,N′,O,O′,ON,ON′]-, ammonium, (OC-6-21)-\n(Ferric ammonium EDTA)\n\nChemical structure and molecular formula\n\nImage\n\nC_{10}H_{16}FeN_{3}O_{8}\n\nMolecular weight^{ a  }(g/mol): 362.09\n\n^{a }Molecular weights were obtained from the ChemIDplus database.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAdenosine triphosphate disodium salt | C10H14N5Na2O13P3 | CID 12822649 - PubChem (https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/Adenosine-triphosphate-disodium-salt)\nciteturn77search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; Adenosine triphosphate disodium\n\nhttps://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?\n\n## 13 Information Sources\n\nFilter by Source[Select]\n\n  1. ChEBI\n\nAdenosine triphosphate disodium\n\nhttps://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:50732\n\nChEBI Ontology\n\nhttps://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/\n\n  2. Dietary Supplement Label Database (DSLD)\n\nLICENSE\n\nDSLD data are in the public domain and they are not copyrighted. They are published under CC0 1.0 Universal (CC0 1.0 ) (https://c