e%20disodium\n\nValue name: Record Description\n\nValue qualifier: Ontology Summary\n\n#### Source\n\nSource: ChEBI\n\nSource ID: CHEBI:OBO:20712\n\nSource record name: Adenosine 5'-phosphate disodium\n\nSource description: Chemical Entities of Biological Interest (ChEBI) is a database and ontology of molecular entities focused on 'small' chemical compounds, that is part of the Open Biomedical Ontologies effort. The term \"molecular entity\" refers to any constitutionally or isotopically distinct atom, molecule, ion, ion pair, radical, radical ion, complex, conformer, etc., identifiable as a separately distinguishable entity.\n\nURL: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:81690\n\n### Toxicity Summary\n\nSafe in the present practices of use and concentration. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nScreening Assessment Report Template (https://www.canada.ca/content/dam/eccc/documents/pdf/pded/edta-salts/EN-FSAR-EDTA-Salts-20180503.pdf)\nciteturn77search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.5 years ago; Crawled: 8.5 years ago; CAS RN 60-00-4 is EDTA and has four acetic acid groups, CAS RN 64-02-8 is a sodium salt of EDTA, CAS RN 15708-41-5 is a ferric salt of EDTA, and CAS RN 21265-50-9 is a ferric ammonium salt of EDTA.\n## 2. Identity of substances\n\nThe Chemical Abstracts Service Registry Numbers (CAS RN³), Domestic Substances List (DSL) names and common names and/or acronyms for the individual substances in the EDTA and its salts group are presented in Table 2-1.\n\nThe four substances within this group all have the same ethylenediamine backbone with carboxylic acid groups on the amine that enable chelation or sequestration of metal ions. CAS RN 60-00-4 is EDTA and has four acetic acid groups, CAS RN 64-02-8 is a sodium salt of EDTA, CAS RN 15708-41-5 is a ferric salt of EDTA, and CAS RN 21265-50-9 is a ferric ammonium salt of EDTA.\n\n**Table 2-1. Substance identities**\n\n<table id=\"e1\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<t